# Requests against the Atlas sample (dotnet run --project samples/Atlas.Api).
# Each one matches something the OpenAPI documents say; the comment says what.

@host = http://localhost:5290

### The documents themselves
GET {{host}}/openapi/locations.json

###
GET {{host}}/openapi/locations-admin.json

### Anonymous: no lock in the docs
GET {{host}}/api/countries

### A CountryId route parameter, documented as a uuid string (Ukraine, a seeded id)
GET {{host}}/api/countries/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### A CityId route parameter, documented as an int32
GET {{host}}/api/cities/1

### [AsParameters] filters: arrays of IDs and codes, each with uniqueItems
GET {{host}}/api/cities?codes=UA&codes=JP&minPopulation=1000000

### The same, by country ids (Ukraine and Chile)
GET {{host}}/api/cities?countryIds=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001&countryIds=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003

### 400: codes lists UA twice ([DistinctItems], "No item may appear twice.")
# Every 400 below is the HttpValidationProblemDetails the documents list (AddValidationProblems).
GET {{host}}/api/cities?codes=UA&codes=UA

### 400: the cross-field rule on SearchCitiesQuery, shown in the operation's description
GET {{host}}/api/cities?minPopulation=10&maxPopulation=1

### 401: the lock in the docs means it
POST {{host}}/api/cities/suggestions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "countryId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001", "name": "Odesa" }

### 400 as a signed-in user: [NotDefault] on countryId ("Must not be the empty id.")
POST {{host}}/api/cities/suggestions
Authorization: Bearer demo-user
Content-Type: application/json

{ "countryId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "name": "Odesa" }

### 202
POST {{host}}/api/cities/suggestions
Authorization: Bearer demo-user
Content-Type: application/json

{ "countryId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001", "name": "Odesa" }

### 403: a user, not an admin
POST {{host}}/api/admin/countries
Authorization: Bearer demo-user
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "PL", "name": "Poland", "continent": "Europe" }

### 400 with the API key (admin document only): [CountryCode] and [DistinctItems]
POST {{host}}/api/admin/countries
X-Api-Key: demo-admin-key
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "pol", "name": "Poland", "continent": "Europe", "borders": ["UA", "UA"] }

### 201 as an admin
POST {{host}}/api/admin/countries
Authorization: Bearer demo-admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "PL", "name": "Poland", "continent": "Europe", "borders": ["UA", "DE"] }

### Anonymous, though the admin group requires the admin policy: AllowAnonymous(), no lock
GET {{host}}/api/admin/status
